# Paths the harness guard protects: a pull request that changes, renames or deletes one of them fails
# the "harness-guard" check until a maintainer approves it with the harness-change-approved label.
#
# One pattern per line; `*` matches across folders. These files decide what "passing" means or what
# agents may do, so weakening them would let a change pass on the weakened rules. Add the files your
# stack's verification depends on (for example `package.json`, if verify.sh calls its scripts).
# This file is itself protected, and CI always reads the copy on main, never the pull request's.

.github/*
.claude/settings.json
.claude/hooks/*
.claude/agents/*
.agents/skills/conformance-review/*
scripts/verify.sh
scripts/secret-scan.sh
scripts/harness-guard.sh
scripts/test/*
REVIEW.md
CODING_STANDARDS.md
